1
00:00:04,560 --> 00:00:05,540
- Hey, guys. - Hey.

2
00:00:05,590 --> 00:00:06,960
- Hi. - Hey.

3
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:09,420
We need to talk about something.

4
00:00:09,470 --> 00:00:10,790
Yeah. We don't feel like

5
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:12,490
we can host Thanksgiving this year.

6
00:00:12,670 --> 00:00:14,430
- What... - Are you kidding?

7
00:00:14,480 --> 00:00:17,480
Well, it's just with work and the stress of adoption...

8
00:00:17,530 --> 00:00:19,470
...we don't feel like we have the energy.

9
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:20,670
Plus, we don't think it's fair

10
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:23,070
that every year the burden falls on us.

11
00:00:24,090 --> 00:00:26,030
That doesn't sound like you.

12
00:00:27,520 --> 00:00:29,500
That's Monica talking.

13
00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:34,160
No, no, we made this decision together.

14
00:00:34,210 --> 00:00:36,240
She's putting words in your mouth.

15
00:00:36,650 --> 00:00:38,350
Don't you put words in people's mouths.

16
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:40,160
You put turkey in people's mouths.

17
00:00:41,480 --> 00:00:42,690
I can't believe this.

18
00:00:42,740 --> 00:00:44,840
This is Emma's first Thanksgiving.

19
00:00:44,970 --> 00:00:46,210
No, it's not.

20
00:00:46,260 --> 00:00:48,550
It's not? When was she born?

21
00:00:50,830 --> 00:00:51,850
Well, personally,

22
00:00:51,900 --> 00:00:54,020
I think it's great you're giving yourself a break.

23
00:00:54,070 --> 00:00:55,420
Thank you, Pheebs.

24
00:00:55,470 --> 00:00:56,860
Sure. It's just as well.

25
00:00:57,010 --> 00:00:58,480
I mean, last year wasn't very good.

26
00:00:58,530 --> 00:01:00,140
I think she's losing her touch.

27
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:03,750
What? You are way off, lady.

28
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:05,330
Am l? Really? Am l?

29
00:01:05,380 --> 00:01:07,250
Well, why don't you cook Thanksgiving dinner

30
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:08,550
and prove me wrong.

31
00:01:10,060 --> 00:01:11,700
Well, think about it.

32
00:01:11,750 --> 00:01:13,910
You'd be trying to top what you did last year.

33
00:01:13,960 --> 00:01:16,680
You'd be in competition with yourself.

34
00:01:18,470 --> 00:01:19,900
That's my favorite kind.

35
00:01:20,790 --> 00:01:22,840
Okay, we are doing this.

36
00:01:23,230 --> 00:01:25,650
Don't let yourself get manipulated this way.

37
00:01:25,700 --> 00:01:27,050
Stay out of this, Chandler.

38
00:01:27,100 --> 00:01:29,190
This is between me and me.

39
00:01:30,880 --> 00:01:32,040
We are supposed to

40
00:01:32,090 --> 00:01:33,630
make these decisions together.

41
00:01:34,850 --> 00:01:37,270
Did you not watch the Dr. Phil I taped for you?

42
00:01:39,540 --> 00:01:41,780
Friends S10E08 The One With The Late Thanksgiving

43
00:02:32,120 --> 00:02:34,170
- Hey. - Hi. Happy Thanksgiving.

44
00:02:34,220 --> 00:02:36,690
Happy Needless Turkey-Murder Day.

45
00:02:38,210 --> 00:02:39,920
You guys, I ordered some chocolate pies

46
00:02:39,970 --> 00:02:41,500
from that bakery on Bleeker.

47
00:02:41,550 --> 00:02:42,550
Could you pick them up for me?

48
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:44,360
You're not making the pies?

49
00:02:44,410 --> 00:02:45,860
I don't make chocolate pies.

50
00:02:45,910 --> 00:02:46,810
When I was younger,

51
00:02:46,860 --> 00:02:48,970
I entered this pie-eating contest.

52
00:02:49,020 --> 00:02:50,010
I ate so many

53
00:02:50,060 --> 00:02:51,710
that the thought of them makes me sick.

54
00:02:51,760 --> 00:02:53,590
Did you at least win the contest?

55
00:02:53,640 --> 00:02:56,540
Two minutes, twelve pies and a part of one tin.

56
00:02:57,920 --> 00:02:59,240
Okay, I'll see you guys at 4.

57
00:02:59,290 --> 00:03:00,300
Can't wait.

58
00:03:00,350 --> 00:03:02,680
This dinner is gonna be so great.

59
00:03:02,730 --> 00:03:04,940
In your face, last-year me.

60
00:03:06,930 --> 00:03:07,990
- Hey, Rach? - Yeah.

61
00:03:08,040 --> 00:03:09,550
What's Emma doing today?

62
00:03:10,080 --> 00:03:11,170
Well, let's see,

63
00:03:11,220 --> 00:03:14,060
I know that she has a meeting with her lawyer...

64
00:03:14,110 --> 00:03:16,870
...and then she has to make a very big poop.

65
00:03:18,820 --> 00:03:19,690
Why?

66
00:03:19,740 --> 00:03:22,280
Well, I want to enter her in a baby pageant.

67
00:03:22,330 --> 00:03:23,610
Oh, my God.

68
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:26,090
That's the creepiest thing I've ever heard.

69
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:28,550
Okay, but before you say no,

70
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:30,510
my friend Suzanne is entering her kid.

71
00:03:30,560 --> 00:03:31,400
And compared to Emma,

72
00:03:31,450 --> 00:03:33,090
she's a real dog.

73
00:03:33,690 --> 00:03:36,120
Phoebe, all babies are beautiful.

74
00:03:36,170 --> 00:03:36,990
Oh, okay.

75
00:03:37,040 --> 00:03:38,690
No. Phoebe,

76
00:03:38,740 --> 00:03:41,700
just the idea of pitting one baby against another...

77
00:03:41,750 --> 00:03:42,950
...l mean, you know,

78
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,990
and judging who's cuter just for a trophy...

79
00:03:45,040 --> 00:03:46,060
And a thousand dollars.

80
00:03:46,110 --> 00:03:49,030
...is something I'm very interested in.

81
00:03:50,110 --> 00:03:52,740
Oh, please, do not tell Ross.

82
00:03:52,790 --> 00:03:53,750
He still believes that

83
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:55,560
what's on the inside is important.

84
00:03:55,610 --> 00:03:58,640
Okay. And Emma needs a cowgirl outfit

85
00:03:58,690 --> 00:03:59,840
for the competition.

86
00:03:59,890 --> 00:04:02,600
Where am I gonna get a cowgirl outfit on Thanksgiving?

87
00:04:02,650 --> 00:04:03,870
Well, I was thinking--

88
00:04:03,920 --> 00:04:06,430
Take the clothes off Joey's Cabbage Patch Kid!

89
00:04:16,410 --> 00:04:18,260
Did someone drop the baton again?

90
00:04:18,310 --> 00:04:20,240
Why come all the way from Kansas

91
00:04:20,290 --> 00:04:21,340
to do that?

92
00:04:24,550 --> 00:04:27,130
I don't get older, I just get better.

93
00:04:28,460 --> 00:04:30,090
You know what just occurred to me?

94
00:04:30,140 --> 00:04:31,660
This could be our last Thanksgiving

95
00:04:31,710 --> 00:04:32,890
just the two of us.

96
00:04:32,940 --> 00:04:35,220
I mean, we could be getting a baby soon.

97
00:04:35,270 --> 00:04:36,130
You don't know that.

98
00:04:36,180 --> 00:04:37,800
Somebody's gonna pick us.

99
00:04:37,850 --> 00:04:38,940
But we haven't heard a thing

100
00:04:38,990 --> 00:04:40,760
from the adoption agency.

101
00:04:40,810 --> 00:04:42,950
I'm telling you, it's gonna happen.

102
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:43,960
Next year,

103
00:04:44,010 --> 00:04:46,930
it's gonna be you, me and little Hemingway Bing.

104
00:04:48,970 --> 00:04:50,620
What? He's my favorite author.

105
00:04:50,670 --> 00:04:52,020
Name one of his books.

106
00:04:57,960 --> 00:04:59,030
The Firm?

107
00:05:00,990 --> 00:05:03,510
Okay, let's see. Okay, the turkey's in the oven.

108
00:05:03,560 --> 00:05:04,750
The stuffing is ready.

109
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:05,300
You know,

110
00:05:05,350 --> 00:05:07,540
you always cook this meal all by yourself.

111
00:05:07,590 --> 00:05:08,950
Let me help this year.

112
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:10,690
Oh, Chandler, that's sweet.

113
00:05:10,740 --> 00:05:13,520
But you don't have to do everything Dr. Phil tells you to do.

114
00:05:14,490 --> 00:05:16,530
I'm serious, let me do something.

115
00:05:16,580 --> 00:05:19,630
Just not the turkey. Nothing high-profile.

116
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:21,400
Okay, let's see.

117
00:05:21,450 --> 00:05:23,030
Oh, the cranberry sauce.

118
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:23,870
It's easy to make,

119
00:05:23,920 --> 00:05:25,530
and no one really cares about it.

120
00:05:26,890 --> 00:05:27,870
Tell me more.

121
00:05:28,200 --> 00:05:30,660
I'm gonna go check on something across the hall.

122
00:05:30,710 --> 00:05:32,440
You start by washing these.

123
00:05:34,980 --> 00:05:36,340
Not with soap!

124
00:05:40,420 --> 00:05:44,080
You obviously haven't tasted my Palmolive potatoes.

125
00:05:46,210 --> 00:05:48,030
Hi. Hey, guess what Joey has.

126
00:05:48,080 --> 00:05:50,060
Three tickets to today's Rangers game!

127
00:05:50,110 --> 00:05:52,030
Dude, I wanted him to guess.

128
00:05:53,020 --> 00:05:54,040
Oh, my God.

129
00:05:54,090 --> 00:05:55,780
Yeah, they're great seats too.

130
00:05:55,830 --> 00:05:56,620
Guess where they are.

131
00:05:56,670 --> 00:05:57,520
Center ice.

132
00:05:59,740 --> 00:06:01,800
Did I do something to you?

133
00:06:04,150 --> 00:06:05,550
The game's at 1.

134
00:06:05,550 --> 00:06:06,240
So?

135
00:06:06,290 --> 00:06:08,020
Dinner's at 4. We'll never make it back.

136
00:06:08,070 --> 00:06:09,310
So we'll leave before it's over.

137
00:06:09,360 --> 00:06:10,130
We'll be back in time.

138
00:06:10,180 --> 00:06:10,980
You said that now.

139
00:06:11,030 --> 00:06:13,240
But it could take us a long time to get back home.

140
00:06:13,290 --> 00:06:14,580
Plus, Joey could get lost

141
00:06:14,630 --> 00:06:16,900
and they could have to page us to go pick him up.

142
00:06:18,580 --> 00:06:20,670
Dude, two times that happened!

143
00:06:22,380 --> 00:06:24,770
Look, Monica's been working hard all day.

144
00:06:24,820 --> 00:06:26,650
She didn't want to host in the first place.

145
00:06:26,700 --> 00:06:27,730
We shouldn't go.

146
00:06:27,870 --> 00:06:29,230
He's right, man.

147
00:06:29,280 --> 00:06:31,550
Yeah, I guess. So we'll see you at 4.

148
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:32,170
Okay.

149
00:06:32,220 --> 00:06:33,310
And get ready to taste

150
00:06:33,360 --> 00:06:35,180
my very special cranberries.

151
00:06:35,670 --> 00:06:38,730
Or should I say "Chan-berries"?

152
00:06:42,770 --> 00:06:44,670
That's some gentle comedy, dude.

153
00:06:46,540 --> 00:06:48,280
We're still going to the game, right?

154
00:06:48,330 --> 00:06:49,080
Yeah.

155
00:06:58,040 --> 00:06:58,620
Hey.

156
00:06:58,670 --> 00:07:00,330
Phoebe, listen, I think we gotta go.

157
00:07:00,380 --> 00:07:01,910
This place is freaking me out.

158
00:07:01,960 --> 00:07:03,370
I've been watching this guy over there.

159
00:07:03,420 --> 00:07:05,030
I don't think he came with a kid.

160
00:07:06,030 --> 00:07:07,610
But we can't leave now.

161
00:07:07,660 --> 00:07:09,160
There was this one baby, Haley,

162
00:07:09,210 --> 00:07:10,080
who was favored to win...

163
00:07:10,130 --> 00:07:12,230
...she got croup, so she had to stay home.

164
00:07:12,280 --> 00:07:15,010
This competition just blew wide-open, folks.

165
00:07:15,800 --> 00:07:18,010
Phoebe, it's just too weird.

166
00:07:18,060 --> 00:07:20,690
I just saw a 1 -year-old with pantyhose on.

167
00:07:20,740 --> 00:07:23,110
Oh, I know. We should've been more prepared.

168
00:07:25,010 --> 00:07:26,780
It's okay. Now, the way I see it,

169
00:07:26,830 --> 00:07:29,270
our real competition now is Cameron.

170
00:07:29,320 --> 00:07:31,310
My God, they just took her sweater off.

171
00:07:31,360 --> 00:07:33,490
Look at those arms. Hello, Michelin Man.

172
00:07:33,540 --> 00:07:35,880
Phoebe, come on.

173
00:07:35,930 --> 00:07:37,710
You know what, it's already 3:00.

174
00:07:37,760 --> 00:07:39,400
They haven't even gotten to Emma's group yet.

175
00:07:39,450 --> 00:07:40,850
We got dinner.

176
00:07:40,900 --> 00:07:42,340
But Emma's got what it takes.

177
00:07:42,390 --> 00:07:43,620
She could go all the way!

178
00:07:46,170 --> 00:07:48,460
Phoebe, you have to calm down.

179
00:07:49,040 --> 00:07:49,880
Okay.

180
00:07:50,260 --> 00:07:53,560
Rachel, the hottest babies in the tri-state area

181
00:07:53,610 --> 00:07:55,940
are in this room right now.

182
00:07:57,650 --> 00:07:59,340
I overheard a judge say

183
00:07:59,390 --> 00:08:01,380
that not one of them holds a candle to Emma.

184
00:08:01,690 --> 00:08:03,150
- Really? - Yeah.

185
00:08:03,200 --> 00:08:04,820
You heard him say that?

186
00:08:04,870 --> 00:08:05,610
Yeah.

187
00:08:06,110 --> 00:08:08,200
All right. Okay. All right,

188
00:08:08,250 --> 00:08:10,420
let's give these babies something to cry about.

189
00:08:10,470 --> 00:08:13,100
Good. Let's get down to business.

190
00:08:13,150 --> 00:08:14,330
Emma needs some makeup.

191
00:08:14,380 --> 00:08:15,460
What?

192
00:08:15,510 --> 00:08:18,170
She's gonna look washed-out next to the others.

193
00:08:18,220 --> 00:08:20,620
No, Phoebe, I'm not letting you put makeup on my baby.

194
00:08:20,670 --> 00:08:21,390
Why not?

195
00:08:21,440 --> 00:08:22,810
Because I already did.

196
00:08:29,920 --> 00:08:33,880
You suck! Get off the ice, you idiot!

197
00:08:34,890 --> 00:08:37,110
- What a game. - I know. Yeah.

198
00:08:37,730 --> 00:08:39,600
I can't believe Chandler's missing this.

199
00:08:39,650 --> 00:08:40,970
I'm sorry he's not here.

200
00:08:41,020 --> 00:08:41,910
But I gotta say,

201
00:08:41,960 --> 00:08:44,350
I am really enjoying nacho chair.

202
00:08:45,450 --> 00:08:47,040
Yeah, I'd probably enjoy it more

203
00:08:47,090 --> 00:08:49,000
if you didn't keep batting my hand away.

204
00:08:51,560 --> 00:08:53,180
These seats are great.

205
00:08:53,230 --> 00:08:54,180
I know, I know.

206
00:08:54,230 --> 00:08:56,460
When I was here for "Holidays on lce" ...

207
00:08:57,840 --> 00:08:59,450
...l was sitting so far away,

208
00:08:59,500 --> 00:09:01,870
Michelle Kwan couldn't read my banner.

209
00:09:03,100 --> 00:09:04,410
We'd better get going.

210
00:09:04,410 --> 00:09:05,840
If we don't leave now, we're gonna be late.

211
00:09:05,840 --> 00:09:07,490
But it's a tie game.

212
00:09:07,540 --> 00:09:08,870
So we're a little late.

213
00:09:08,920 --> 00:09:10,290
The girls will be there.

214
00:09:10,340 --> 00:09:12,420
Let's just stay for one more goal.

215
00:09:12,470 --> 00:09:14,090
- I don't know. - One more fight.

216
00:09:14,140 --> 00:09:15,350
- Okay. - Okay.

217
00:09:19,760 --> 00:09:21,010
Where is everybody?

218
00:09:21,060 --> 00:09:22,220
They're 45 minutes late.

219
00:09:22,270 --> 00:09:23,900
I can't believe they're not here.

220
00:09:23,950 --> 00:09:26,410
I slave and I slave for what?

221
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:29,650
They've ruined Cranberry Day.

222
00:09:31,900 --> 00:09:33,250
How late are we?

223
00:09:33,250 --> 00:09:34,090
Forty-five minutes.

224
00:09:34,140 --> 00:09:36,440
- Here. - Okay.

225
00:09:37,230 --> 00:09:39,030
Rachel and Phoebe are already there,

226
00:09:39,080 --> 00:09:40,280
so they probably started without us.

227
00:09:40,330 --> 00:09:41,620
We could just slip in,

228
00:09:41,670 --> 00:09:43,090
and no one needs to know where we were.

229
00:09:45,090 --> 00:09:47,580
You may want to lose the foam finger.

230
00:09:47,630 --> 00:09:49,540
Oh, no, no, no.

231
00:09:49,590 --> 00:09:51,290
You just want to put it on your hand.

232
00:09:55,130 --> 00:09:57,220
You're not at Thanksgiving?

233
00:09:57,270 --> 00:09:58,960
No, we're late.

234
00:09:59,010 --> 00:10:00,540
What are you doing here?

235
00:10:00,590 --> 00:10:01,980
We're late too.

236
00:10:02,770 --> 00:10:03,940
We figured we could be late

237
00:10:03,990 --> 00:10:05,560
because you'd be on time.

238
00:10:05,610 --> 00:10:07,820
Don't point that thing at me, Tribbiani.

239
00:10:08,700 --> 00:10:10,290
So nobody's here?

240
00:10:10,340 --> 00:10:11,650
Monica's gonna kill us.

241
00:10:11,700 --> 00:10:12,880
Yeah, where were you?

242
00:10:12,930 --> 00:10:14,910
Yeah, what's with the trophy?

243
00:10:14,960 --> 00:10:17,920
Well, we were at a spelling bee.

244
00:10:19,650 --> 00:10:21,000
And I won.

245
00:10:22,230 --> 00:10:23,800
You won an adult

246
00:10:23,850 --> 00:10:26,410
Thanksgiving Day spelling bee?

247
00:10:26,930 --> 00:10:29,660
Yes. Y-E-S. Yes.

248
00:10:30,170 --> 00:10:32,060
Let me see this.

249
00:10:32,290 --> 00:10:35,750
"Grand Supreme Little Darling, New York Division"?

250
00:10:35,800 --> 00:10:37,170
That's me.

251
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:42,080
You entered Emma in a beauty pageant?

252
00:10:42,870 --> 00:10:46,150
And it looks like she put makeup on her.

253
00:10:47,240 --> 00:10:48,680
Wait a second...

254
00:10:48,730 --> 00:10:51,440
Where have I seen that cowgirl outfit before?

255
00:10:52,580 --> 00:10:53,850
I can't believe this.

256
00:10:53,900 --> 00:10:55,110
She's our daughter.

257
00:10:55,160 --> 00:10:57,760
That you would treat her like some kind of show dog

258
00:10:57,810 --> 00:10:58,990
is inexcusable.

259
00:10:59,040 --> 00:11:00,580
She won a thousand dollars.

260
00:11:00,630 --> 00:11:02,940
So this is an annual thing?

261
00:11:06,730 --> 00:11:09,000
That's Alicia May Emory's outfit!

262
00:11:10,870 --> 00:11:12,490
Guys, there are people in there

263
00:11:12,540 --> 00:11:13,980
who are not getting any happier.

264
00:11:14,100 --> 00:11:15,320
What are we gonna do?

265
00:11:15,370 --> 00:11:16,500
I don't know, you guys figure it out.

266
00:11:16,550 --> 00:11:17,730
I gotta put Emma down for a nap.

267
00:11:17,780 --> 00:11:19,190
And, Rach, while you're in there,

268
00:11:19,190 --> 00:11:20,740
throw something on Alicia May.

269
00:11:22,840 --> 00:11:24,480
All right, what are we gonna say?

270
00:11:24,530 --> 00:11:27,140
We'll say that we were mugged.

271
00:11:27,190 --> 00:11:29,080
You can't get mad at someone

272
00:11:29,130 --> 00:11:30,330
who's been mugged.

273
00:11:30,380 --> 00:11:32,480
Good. But you don't look like you were mugged.

274
00:11:32,530 --> 00:11:33,950
No. Here.

